{"name":"Rosenkavalier","hex":"#bc8a90","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Der Rosenkavalier","blocks":[{"text":"Der Rosenkavalier, Op. 59, is a comic opera in three acts by Richard Strauss to an original German libretto by Hugo von Hofmannsthal. It is loosely adapted from Louvet de Couvrai's novel Les amours du chevalier de Faublas and Molière's comedy Monsieur de Pourceaugnac. It was first performed at the Königliches Opernhaus in Dresden on 26 January 1911 under the direction of Max Reinhardt, with Ernst von Schuch conducting. Until the premiere, the working title was Ochs auf Lerchenau."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Robert_Sterl_Schuch_dirigiert_Rosenkavalier.jpg/330px-Robert_Sterl_Schuch_dirigiert_Rosenkavalier.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Der_Rosenkavalier"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Postcard-1910_Strauss_Richard.jpg/500px-Postcard-1910_Strauss_Richard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Postcard-1910_Strauss_Richard.jpg/1280px-Postcard-1910_Strauss_Richard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Postcard-1910_Strauss_Richard.jpg/500px-Postcard-1910_Strauss_Richard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Richard Strauss in 1910","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APostcard-1910_Strauss_Richard.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Renato_Ercolani_come_Valzacchi_in_%22Der_Rosenkavalier%22%2C_Salzburger_Festspiele_1960_-_collezione_Tino_Barindelli.tiff/lossy-page1-500px-Renato_Ercolani_come_Valzacchi_in_%22Der_Rosenkavalier%22%2C_Salzburger_Festspiele_1960_-_collezione_Tino_